WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.870
Drop a strip of zinc into dilute
hydrochloric acid, and it fizzes.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.490
Dip a gold ring into the same
acid, and nothing happens.

3
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.450
Not a single bubble.

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.290
Both are metals, sitting in the same acid.

5
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.090
So what makes the difference?

6
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:18.710
Why does zinc fizz in acid,
when a gold ring doesn't?

7
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.770
In this mission, you'll follow the trends
in how readily metals and halogens react.

8
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.370
You'll predict displacement reactions,

9
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.510
and write equations for
metals reacting with acids.

10
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.960
Your mission: explain why zinc
fizzes in acid but gold doesn't.
